't agree.** The 7/1 message says it was closed, but the 9/30 digest has Mateo submitting it as new. That digest also says Newark and Door 14, while the earlier mentions say Allentown. That could be a reused ticket number or an error in the digest. I'd confirm it with Gideon.\n- **#PD-4418 may not be Vantorre Group.** That digest only says \"the account Nadia runs\" and never names Vantorre. I included it because it's the likely fit, but I can't confirm it.\n- **Other digests mention Vantorre Group but give no ticket number.** These are 3/10/2025, 7/7/2025, 5/3/2026 and 8/3/2026. The 8/3/2026 one covers the Hartford incident and a customer explanation for Mateo. The 12/1/2025 digest is Mobility only.\n- **The 8/3 digest lists no ticket for the door-assignment and duplicate check-in complaints.** I couldn't tie them to a ticket number.\n- **I haven't seen the tickets themselves.** The list comes only from the pod channel, #inc-vtg-hartford and Moss's strategic digests. I can't see Pemberline's support system, so there may be tickets that were never mentioned in those places."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
